y). Anonymous is deliberately excluded: every invocation builds a computer, and at an open door that is unmetered cost any stranger could repeat.\",\n \"supersedes\": null,\n \"status\": \"pending\",\n \"recipe_id\": null,\n \"log\": null,\n \"verb\": {\n  \"name\": \"page_title\",\n  \"description\": \"Fetch an http(s) URL on a fresh computer and report the text of the page's <title> element. Prints the title on stdout; on failure prints a reason on stderr and exits non-zero (2 bad scheme, 3 no title, 5 fetch failed, 6 HTTP >= 400).\",\n  \"params\": {\n   \"properties\": {\n    \"url\": {\n     \"description\": \"The http:// or https:// URL of the page whose title should be reported.\",\n     \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n   },\n   \"required\": [\n    \"url\"\n   ],\n   \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"dockerfile\": \"FROM mshkn-base\\nRUN mkdir -p /verb && printf '#!/bin/sh\\\\nperl -0777 -pe \\\"s{<!--.*?-->}{}gs; s{<script.*?</script>}{}gis; s{<style.*?</style>}{}gis\\\" | tr \\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\t\\\" \\\"   \\\" | grep -oi \\\"<title[^>]*>[^<]*\\\" | head -n1 | sed \\\"s/^<[Tt][Ii][Tt][Ll][Ee][^>]*>//\\\" | sed -e \\\"s/&nbsp;/ /g\\\" -e \\\"s/&quot;/\\\\\\\\\\\"/g\\\" -e \\\"s/&#39;/\\\\\\\\x27/g\\\" -e \\\"s/&#x27;/\\\\\\\\x27/g\\\" -e \\\"s/&lt;/</g\\\" -e \\\"s/&gt;/>/g\\\" -e \\\"s/&amp;/\\\\\\\\&/g\\\" | tr -s \\\" \\\" | sed -e \\\"s/^ *//\\\" -e \\\"s/ *$//\\\"\\\\n' > /verb/extract.sh && chmod +x /verb/extract.sh\\nRUN printf '#!/bin/sh\\\\nset -u\\\\nurl=\\\"$1\\\"\\\\ncase \\\"$url\\\" in\\\\n  http://*|https://*) ;;\\\\n  *) echo \\\"error: only http and https URLs are supported\\\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\\\\nesac\\\\nmeta=$(curl -sS -L --max-redirs 5 --max-time 20 --max-filesize 5000000 -o /tmp/body -w \\\"%%{http_code} %%{content_type}\\\" -A \\\"mshkn-page-title/1\\\" -H \\\"Accept: text/html\\\" \\\"$url\\\" 2>/tmp/err)\\\\nrc=$?\\\\nif [ \\\"$rc\\\" -ne 0 ]; then printf \\\"error: fetch failed: %%s\\\\\\\\n\\\" \\\"$(head -c 200 /tmp/err)\\\"